WEBVTT

00:04.230 --> 00:08.470
<b>Starting this year, there is a change in the
Logos Registration Card renewal procedures.</b>

00:08.470 --> 00:10.510
<b>To prevent an influx of Revinus refugees,</b>

00:10.510 --> 00:15.440
<b>the term of validity has been reduced from five years
to three, and identities will be thoroughly checked.</b>

00:15.740 --> 00:20.010
Hey, you know, maybe I'll stay over at
your place tonight, Hideki.

00:20.950 --> 00:22.850
Really? You sure?

00:24.590 --> 00:25.550
What's going on all of sudden?

00:26.150 --> 00:28.090
Hey, what's going on?

00:28.090 --> 00:29.380
<b>ATS SUSPENDED</b>

00:28.220 --> 00:29.590
Looks like traffic's stopped.

00:29.760 --> 00:30.730
It's dark.

00:30.730 --> 00:31.590
The power's out?

00:31.590 --> 00:33.620
I've never heard of such a thing!

00:46.880 --> 01:00.250
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi tobitate tsubasa de

00:46.880 --> 00:53.490
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

00:53.490 --> 01:00.260
Take flight on wings

01:14.600 --> 01:17.770
Morokute nigai kajitsu no you ni

01:14.610 --> 01:17.780
Like fragile but bitter fruit

01:17.770 --> 01:20.980
Hito no kokoro o miryou suru no

01:17.780 --> 01:20.990
It fascinates people's hearts

01:20.980 --> 01:24.080
Togi sumasareta shiroi yubi de

01:20.990 --> 01:22.490
The shadow that manipulates

01:22.490 --> 01:24.090
With sharpened fingers gleaming white

01:24.080 --> 01:27.250
Ayatsuru kage wa chi no kaori

01:24.090 --> 01:27.260
Smells of blood

01:27.250 --> 01:40.250
Shizumi aseta kodou o yobi samasu shi no sasayaki

01:27.260 --> 01:33.700
The whisper of Death

01:33.700 --> 01:40.260
That awakens fading heartbeats

01:41.230 --> 01:47.600
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi

01:41.240 --> 01:47.610
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

01:47.600 --> 01:53.840
Tobitatsu no wa gin no tsubasa

01:47.610 --> 01:53.850
Silver wings take flight

01:53.840 --> 02:00.320
Fukai kaze ni tsume o tatete

01:53.850 --> 02:00.320
Become the power that tears at deep winds

02:00.320 --> 02:10.050
Kirisaku chikara to nare

02:00.320 --> 02:10.060
With poised claws

02:11.020 --> 02:14.270
Brought to you by
BiG-GuY Fansubbing

02:26.880 --> 02:31.210
Episode 2
Madness

02:31.210 --> 02:34.920
The terrorists who have taken over the
Revinus area Nuclear Power Plant Number 6

02:34.920 --> 02:38.780
have, as previously warned, cut the
supply of electricity to Logos area F7.

02:39.450 --> 02:41.890
Currently, the scene is still at a deadlock,

02:41.890 --> 02:43.950
and there is no predicting how
the situation will play out.

02:55.840 --> 02:58.210
Don't make me repeat myself!

02:58.210 --> 03:01.380
Next time, we'll cut the power supply
on a much larger scale!

03:01.380 --> 03:03.680
And if you still don't meet our demands,

03:03.680 --> 03:05.200
then we'll blow up the power plant!

03:11.290 --> 03:12.980
So they're here.

03:13.120 --> 03:17.430
Who would've thought we'd find ourselves in a
situation where we'd have to ask for their help.

03:17.430 --> 03:18.960
Can't be helped.

03:18.960 --> 03:21.660
If this goes on any longer,
fingers will start pointing.

03:26.270 --> 03:28.100
So many bullets wasted.

03:28.470 --> 03:31.230
Looks like we're dealing with amateurs.

03:31.810 --> 03:32.970
To the Command Center!

03:32.970 --> 03:33.600
Roger.

03:48.720 --> 03:50.280
We've been waiting for you.

03:56.360 --> 03:57.830
Thanks for coming.

03:58.130 --> 03:59.630
What are their demands?

03:59.630 --> 04:01.570
The release of their comrades.

04:02.000 --> 04:09.380
The guys we put in prison for the riots
at Revinus Areas 6 and 18, and Logos Section R7.

04:10.280 --> 04:11.910
And why has it dragged on for this long?

04:11.910 --> 04:13.850
Isn't that obvious?

04:13.850 --> 04:18.010
Given the location, we're restricted
in our use of firearms.

04:18.990 --> 04:21.020
This is the situation.

04:21.020 --> 04:24.690
They're using stolen military weapons
as barricades.

04:25.460 --> 04:27.160
How many are there?

04:27.230 --> 04:32.800
Four in the control room, three on the rooftop,
five in the turbine room.

04:32.800 --> 04:35.140
Due to the proximity to a heat source,
it's difficult to confirm,

04:35.140 --> 04:38.700
but judging by the number of vehicles at the time
of invasion, there must be seven or eight more.

04:39.310 --> 04:43.440
They've kindly sent us an image of the
explosive device via the web.

04:43.750 --> 04:45.080
This is it.

04:45.680 --> 04:48.250
A wireless detonator...

04:48.250 --> 04:51.910
The leader in the control room
has the detonator switch.

04:53.420 --> 04:55.390
We have a communication from the terrorists!

04:57.830 --> 04:59.290
Let me talk to them.

05:00.430 --> 05:01.800
Can you hear me?

05:01.800 --> 05:03.590
I am Renée Vikro.

05:03.670 --> 05:06.690
I will be in charge of negotiations from now on.

05:08.640 --> 05:10.900
A little too late for BS negotiations!

05:11.140 --> 05:13.000
Carry out our demands immediately!

05:13.470 --> 05:16.740
We are already preparing to meet your demands.

05:16.910 --> 05:21.580
Give me a little more time to make arrangements
with the Legal Affairs Bureau and the prisons.

05:22.050 --> 05:24.580
We've given you enough time!

05:24.850 --> 05:26.150
We can't wait any longer!

05:26.150 --> 05:27.180
Wait.

05:28.290 --> 05:31.490
The six prisoners at Prison Number Five
can be transported out.

05:31.490 --> 05:35.520
We'll send a helicopter over right away.
Give me three more hours.

05:35.700 --> 05:37.400
I'll give you two!

05:37.400 --> 05:39.230
If you go over that, then...

05:39.230 --> 05:41.670
You'll blow it up? Is that what you're saying?

05:41.670 --> 05:43.770
That's one of our options.

05:43.770 --> 05:45.770
It's impossible to do in two hours.

05:45.770 --> 05:47.310
I can do it in three, without fail.

05:47.310 --> 05:48.810
Two and a half hours!

05:48.810 --> 05:50.940
Three hours. You got that?

05:51.980 --> 05:53.750
What the hell are you trying to do?!

05:53.750 --> 05:55.770
We haven't made any arrangements
for their release!

05:55.850 --> 05:59.190
This is 1-0 Bravo to Delta 1.

05:59.190 --> 06:00.250
Prepare to attack!

06:00.250 --> 06:02.620
Hold it! What the hell are you thinking?!

06:02.620 --> 06:05.830
Obviously we need to take immediate action.

06:05.830 --> 06:07.330
They are dead serious.

06:07.330 --> 06:09.300
I wouldn't be surprised if they
actually blew the plant up.

06:09.300 --> 06:10.700
What are you basing that on?

06:11.230 --> 06:16.500
The agitated voiceprint leads me to believe that his
mental state has reached a dangerous level.

06:16.670 --> 06:20.480
But even so, it's premature to order an attack!

06:20.480 --> 06:23.680
Don't you see the situation we're in?!

06:23.680 --> 06:26.150
There's no time left for us.

06:26.150 --> 06:29.640
Since you asked us to come here,
I expect you to follow my orders.

06:30.720 --> 06:34.850
My orders as Phantom's Vice-Commander!

06:35.020 --> 06:38.460
Houses blew away, forests blew away.

06:38.460 --> 06:41.960
A wind-swept morning. Nothing's left.

06:41.960 --> 06:45.500
Buildings blew away, mountains blew away.

06:45.500 --> 06:49.160
A weather-beaten night. Nothing's left.

06:51.910 --> 06:52.170
Gora!

06:52.170 --> 06:52.610
Gora!
Mom can't be found. My stomach can't be filled.

06:52.610 --> 06:53.980
Mom can't be found. My stomach can't be filled.

06:53.980 --> 06:55.500
Gora! Which way?
Mom can't be found. My stomach can't be filled.

06:55.780 --> 06:58.180
Huh? Right!

06:58.250 --> 06:59.750
Stay away from me. You stink!

06:59.750 --> 07:00.750
What are you talking about?

07:00.750 --> 07:02.680
I just took a bath a month ago, you know!

07:02.680 --> 07:04.050
Yuck, stay away from me!

07:04.050 --> 07:06.920
Looks like we're taking a pretty roundabout way.

07:06.920 --> 07:10.290
Well, that's what happens when you take
these inconspicuous back roads.

07:10.490 --> 07:12.360
You sure about this, Jin?

07:12.360 --> 07:14.300
Asking someone like Gora to show us the way?

07:14.300 --> 07:17.920
What do you mean "someone like Gora"?
Have a little trust, will ya?

07:18.370 --> 07:21.360
This area's like my backyard.

07:21.870 --> 07:25.570
But more importantly, how about telling me
exactly where you want to go?

07:26.040 --> 07:28.540
As long as you take us to
an area near it, that's fine.

07:28.540 --> 07:31.940
Damn. So you don't trust me after all.

07:36.420 --> 07:39.850
We'll be arriving shortly. Tell us where to land.

07:40.120 --> 07:42.690
Head for the rooftop of the turbine tower.

07:42.690 --> 07:46.030
Turbine tower? All right. I'll have them land there.

07:46.030 --> 07:49.360
Wait! Keep hovering at 10 meters above ground!

07:49.360 --> 07:51.870
From there, show me the faces of my comrades.

07:51.870 --> 07:53.990
I need to confirm that first.

07:54.670 --> 07:55.800
Roger.

08:01.680 --> 08:05.040
What's going on?! I told you to
show me my comrades!

08:05.480 --> 08:08.980
The leader with the wireless detonator
is in the control room.

08:08.980 --> 08:13.820
Due to the danger of radioactive contamination,
using firearms inside is absolutely forbidden.

08:13.820 --> 08:16.560
Change your launchers over to rubber bullets
and deal with it that way.

08:16.560 --> 08:18.430
That is all. Any questions?

08:18.430 --> 08:21.920
How do you know nobody else has a switch?

08:22.530 --> 08:26.020
We've confirmed it by monitoring
the radio wave frequency.

08:26.230 --> 08:28.440
What if we create wireless interference?

08:28.440 --> 08:33.840
We can't. The electromagnetic waves may have
an adverse effect on the reactor's control system.

08:34.080 --> 08:36.410
Yeah, it may just explode in a burst of blue light...

08:37.710 --> 08:39.150
What's the frequency?

08:39.150 --> 08:41.450
5.2 GHz.

08:41.450 --> 08:44.480
All right. We'll go with a #5 chaff grenade.

08:45.250 --> 08:46.890
Commence operation!

08:46.890 --> 08:48.260
Roger!

08:48.260 --> 08:49.920
Hurry up and show me their faces!

09:12.010 --> 09:15.040
<b>We interrupt this program to bring you breaking news.</b>

09:15.780 --> 09:21.350
<b>There has been a new development
in the standoff at the nuclear power plant.</b>

09:22.490 --> 09:27.050
<b>We just received word that a special anti-terrorism force
has stormed the plant.</b>

09:28.060 --> 09:29.790
So they've made their move.

10:26.920 --> 10:28.250
So it's come down to this, huh?

10:31.760 --> 10:33.660
W-why?!

10:34.530 --> 10:37.020
The radio waves have been cut off by the chaff.

10:37.200 --> 10:39.600
Next time, use wires!

10:48.610 --> 10:51.370
This is Delta 1. Mission accomplished.

10:52.650 --> 10:54.440
That was too easy.

11:17.470 --> 11:19.040
Take care of Sana for me.

11:19.040 --> 11:20.010
Yeah.

11:20.010 --> 11:22.110
Jin, let me go with you.

11:22.110 --> 11:25.010
I don't know how it'll be inside.

11:25.010 --> 11:26.670
Wait here, okay?

11:26.780 --> 11:29.250
Jin! Hurry up! Let's go!

11:31.050 --> 11:32.310
Jin...

11:39.560 --> 11:42.290
Damn. There's nothing here.

11:51.840 --> 11:52.930
Joe?

11:55.380 --> 11:58.000
How about saying something?

11:58.680 --> 12:00.110
Why?

12:00.110 --> 12:01.620
I don't know why.

12:01.620 --> 12:04.790
It's just that if you don't say anything, it's, um...

12:04.790 --> 12:06.750
scary, you know?

12:10.690 --> 12:12.220
Like what?

12:13.960 --> 12:16.120
What should I talk about?

12:16.260 --> 12:18.060
Well, about...

12:26.410 --> 12:27.170
Gora's...

12:28.040 --> 12:30.880
Stop that! Don't scare me like that all of a sudden!

12:38.950 --> 12:40.580
Gora's what?

12:43.390 --> 12:45.590
What about Gora?

12:46.860 --> 12:48.950
It's nothing important.

12:56.370 --> 12:57.500
Um...

12:59.110 --> 13:01.600
How long have you been with Jin?

13:02.710 --> 13:04.640
Hey, don't you think Jin is...

13:05.710 --> 13:07.040
Don't move.

13:14.920 --> 13:17.420
This is car 130. We've arrived at the scene.

13:17.420 --> 13:21.160
Container truck confirmed.
We'll start investigating now.

13:21.160 --> 13:22.190
Roger.

13:25.300 --> 13:26.130
No match

13:26.570 --> 13:29.840
No response from the vehicle data
communication device.

13:29.840 --> 13:31.410
It must be unregistered.

13:31.410 --> 13:34.380
That's not unusual in Revinus.

13:34.380 --> 13:36.540
Should we just let it go?

13:36.540 --> 13:41.610
No, we should at least check to see
what it's carrying.

13:42.750 --> 13:44.650
I guess you're right.

13:55.730 --> 13:57.700
Hey, open up!

13:58.000 --> 13:59.500
We got a call!

13:59.500 --> 14:01.870
What are you carrying in such a big truck?

14:01.870 --> 14:03.500
Open up!

14:04.710 --> 14:07.040
Looks like nobody's inside.

14:07.040 --> 14:09.910
I wonder if they went into the supermarket.

14:10.040 --> 14:12.150
What a pain in the ass.

14:12.150 --> 14:14.320
Should we call for backup?

14:14.320 --> 14:17.280
Let's check out what's inside the
container before we do that.

14:26.490 --> 14:28.860
This is great!

14:29.300 --> 14:32.530
Hey, look at this! Corned beef!

14:32.530 --> 14:34.200
And the expiration date...

14:34.200 --> 14:36.000
is only two years ago!

14:36.000 --> 14:38.160
It's just about right to eat now!

14:38.240 --> 14:41.610
Are you kiddin' me? Broiled saury!

14:41.610 --> 14:44.770
Man, I love this place, Jin!

14:55.660 --> 14:56.710
Jin!

15:00.730 --> 15:02.330
Are you okay, Sana?

15:02.330 --> 15:04.300
Yeah. Joe is...

15:09.900 --> 15:13.500
Hey, Jin! Come on, how about helping out a little?

15:16.580 --> 15:19.310
W-what happened here?

15:28.690 --> 15:31.920
We'll soon be at the area where
the SOS signal was sent out.

15:32.790 --> 15:35.660
I wonder if they were attacked
by those punks again.

15:36.930 --> 15:39.730
I don't know yet, but we shouldn't
let our guard down.

15:39.730 --> 15:40.670
Sir!

15:41.040 --> 15:43.560
All hands to Level 1 alert positions!

15:47.310 --> 15:49.110
Flotsam sighted!

15:49.680 --> 15:50.740
Hey!

16:02.890 --> 16:07.090
Survivors spotted.
Commencing rescue operations immediately.

16:08.200 --> 16:10.100
Damned pirates!

16:15.370 --> 16:19.640
Looks like the military hasn't gotten
the report from the police yet.

16:20.040 --> 16:22.010
Should I have just finished them off?

16:22.010 --> 16:23.180
Don't be stupid.

16:23.180 --> 16:26.010
Because they're still alive,
this hasn't become a big deal yet.

16:26.250 --> 16:29.620
They're just dogs controlling Revinus after all.

16:29.620 --> 16:31.550
A bunch of rotten bastards...

16:32.450 --> 16:35.510
In any case, we have no choice
but to go full speed to our destination.

16:44.300 --> 16:45.530
Hey.

16:45.700 --> 16:46.870
Hm?

16:46.870 --> 16:51.170
Tell me. Who the heck are those guys?

16:52.810 --> 16:54.270
I don't know.

16:55.480 --> 16:57.240
Don't hide it.

16:57.240 --> 17:00.480
If you don't know, then why do you stay with them?

17:01.280 --> 17:03.250
Why?

17:07.990 --> 17:10.650
Because I thought they'd protect me...

17:11.760 --> 17:13.560
Who would?

17:18.630 --> 17:21.030
I thought they'd protect me for sure.

17:21.800 --> 17:23.390
Whatever.

17:33.110 --> 17:35.050
It's so pretty!

17:35.050 --> 17:36.620
Look, the ocean! The ocean!

17:36.620 --> 17:39.050
Jeez, what are you, a kid?!

17:39.050 --> 17:41.680
But I've never seen it before!

17:41.890 --> 17:45.130
You have no idea how tense the situation is
right now, do you, Princess?

17:45.130 --> 17:46.960
Is this seriously your first time?

17:46.960 --> 17:51.020
Yes. I never thought it would be this pretty!

17:53.270 --> 17:57.170
I saw it just one time before, from an airplane.

17:57.170 --> 18:00.870
An airplane?! So you've been on one?!

18:01.410 --> 18:05.810
Man, you really are a celebrity, aren't you!

18:06.380 --> 18:09.150
So, how was it? It was pretty high up, wasn't it?

18:09.150 --> 18:10.850
I bet it was really high, huh?

18:10.850 --> 18:12.010
Like super high, right?

18:12.090 --> 18:14.050
Aw, come on. Tell me!

18:14.760 --> 18:16.090
It's a bridge! A bridge!

18:16.090 --> 18:19.690
What's the big deal? Don't get so
excited over just a bridge!

18:19.690 --> 18:22.430
It's a tunnel! A tunnel!

18:22.430 --> 18:24.420
Hey, you're just as bad.

18:35.210 --> 18:38.740
Gora. Do I stay on this road for a while?

18:39.050 --> 18:41.350
There are back roads,

18:41.350 --> 18:44.580
but you can't go on them in a huge truck like this.

18:44.650 --> 18:47.590
But we'll attract attention
on this road, won't we?

18:47.590 --> 18:49.490
Don't worry about it.

18:49.490 --> 18:53.620
If it comes down to it, these two will
protect you, Princess.

18:53.790 --> 18:57.260
Wearing that awesome armor.

18:57.260 --> 19:01.400
I know about it, you know.
That's from the military, isn't it?

19:01.400 --> 19:05.170
Are you two on the run after
stealing that from the military?

19:05.170 --> 19:07.370
Is that why they're after you?

19:07.370 --> 19:08.710
Or maybe it's because...

19:08.710 --> 19:09.510
Jin.

19:10.110 --> 19:11.300
What's wrong?

19:26.260 --> 19:27.560
What on Earth?

19:27.560 --> 19:29.760
Haven't you heard of pirates?

19:29.760 --> 19:30.930
Pirates?

19:30.930 --> 19:32.570
But that ship's a...

19:32.570 --> 19:34.940
No ifs or buts about it.

19:34.940 --> 19:38.040
A buddy of mine's on that ship.

19:38.040 --> 19:41.310
Hand it over to me. Your armor.

19:41.310 --> 19:42.670
Gora! You!

19:43.740 --> 19:46.010
Over here! Over here!

20:07.900 --> 20:09.030
Joe!

20:16.740 --> 20:17.880
It's the military.

20:17.880 --> 20:19.380
Gora! Why you...

20:19.380 --> 20:21.900
D-don't blame me for the military!

20:22.080 --> 20:23.320
Let's go, Joe.

20:23.320 --> 20:25.420
Wait. I'll attract their attention.

20:25.420 --> 20:26.680
But...

20:27.320 --> 20:29.260
Take Sana and run.

20:32.830 --> 20:33.820
All right.

20:34.230 --> 20:34.920
Get out!

21:11.230 --> 21:12.490
Oh, crap!

21:43.000 --> 21:46.520
Things are starting to get interesting.

21:47.070 --> 21:49.730
Hey, open up! Let me on!

22:25.070 --> 22:29.580
Nagai kioku no hate ni

22:25.070 --> 22:29.540
If at the end of our long memory

22:29.540 --> 22:35.380
Time will tear us apart

22:29.580 --> 22:35.410
Toki ga bokura o wakatsu nara

22:37.420 --> 22:44.060
If at the end of my sweet memory with you

22:37.450 --> 22:44.090
Kimi to amai kioku no hate ni

22:44.060 --> 22:50.360
You and I become one again

22:44.090 --> 22:50.400
Mata bokura hitotsu nara

22:50.360 --> 22:57.540
From a quietly stretched arm's length away

22:50.400 --> 22:57.570
Sotto te nobashita kyori kara

22:57.540 --> 23:02.240
I will search for the meaning

22:57.570 --> 23:02.280
lmi o sagasu kara

23:02.240 --> 23:08.080
Can you hear it? The words dance in midair

23:02.280 --> 23:08.120
Kikoeru? Kotoba ga chuu ni mau

23:08.080 --> 23:13.890
We shall meet when our wish is granted

23:08.120 --> 23:13.920
Kanaeta toki ni deau

23:13.890 --> 23:17.560
Leaving only their reverse behind

23:13.920 --> 23:17.590
Reverse dake nokoshite

23:17.560 --> 23:20.960
The torn words

23:17.590 --> 23:20.990
Chigireta kotoba

23:20.960 --> 23:27.090
Blurred time and light

23:20.990 --> 23:27.130
Kasureta jikan to hikari

23:29.270 --> 23:33.600
I have found them now

23:29.300 --> 23:33.640
lma, mitsuketa kara

23:35.190 --> 23:46.190
Next Episode

23:44.820 --> 23:48.620
Next time on Innocent Venus:

23:48.190 --> 23:50.690
Episode 3
Pirates

23:48.620 --> 23:49.890
"Pirates"
